<title>JAPAN: Sanwa shares to be included in Nikkei 225.</title>
<headline>Sanwa shares to be included in Nikkei 225.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Nihon Keizai Shimbun Inc said on Tuesday it would include Sanwa Bank Ltd in its Nikkei Average index of 225 shares from September 24.</p>
<p>Concurrently, Honshu Paper Co Ltd will be delisted from the benchmark index in the Tokyo Stock Exchange.  </p>
<p>Honshu Paper will be removed from the index because it will be delisted from the exchange when its merges with New Oji Paper Co Ltd, the Japanese business daily, which manages the index, said in a statement.</p>
<p>In addition, Nihon Keizai Shimbun said it would remove Honshu Paper and Showa Denko KK from the Nikkei 300 index. They will be replaced by East Japan Railway Co, on September 24, and DDI Corp, on October 1, the paper said.</p>
<p>Honshu Paper will also be deleted from the Nikkei 500 stock average, and will be replaced by Tokin Corp on September 24, the paper said.</p>
</text>
